# tally 2.2.1 (#230, 230.Q4), E §5 step 1: "one known inside the window leaves the amounts HOLE-IMPRECISE where it
# changes them". pay is dated w = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-20); a1 (known 2026-03-08) makes amt 150.00 PLN and a2
# (known 2026-03-12) 100.00 PLN again, so the booking cut gives 100.00, 150.00 and 100.00 PLN on the window's three
# pieces: the amount is the window's hole (undone, undone_f), where pinned days give HOLE-CHANGED holes (u06) or
# 600.00 PLN (u15). tally 2.2 compared the booking cut at the window's two ends only: 600.00 PLN in silence (the
# planner's misc2/m2.tally, less its `before top`, which S-221.9 refuses).
=== m2.tally
model m2
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place sav: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input w: date
input keep: money PLN
input d_at: date
input d_top: date
move pay: transfers
  on w
  at d_at
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt
move top: transfers
  on d_top
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to sav amount max(0 PLN, bal(konto) - keep)
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d_at = 2026-03-01 "s"
  d_top = 2026-04-10 "s"
  keep = 100.00 PLN "s"
  w = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-20) "s"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
  opening[sav] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
version a0
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
version a1
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-03-08
  replace amt = 150.00 PLN "s"
version a2
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-03-12
  replace amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
ask undone: bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
ask undone_f: flows(pay, 2026-03)
ask u06: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) with w = 2026-03-06
ask u15: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) with w = 2026-03-15
=== expect
u06: ?"pay on 2026-03-06 changed after it was paid (version a1); is back pay due, and when?" (pay) ?"pay on 2026-03-06 changed after it was paid (version a2); is back pay due, and when?" (pay)
  pinned: w = 2026-03-06
  adjustment: pay by -50.00 PLN on 2026-03-12 (version a2), remaining -50.00 PLN
  adjustment: pay by 50.00 PLN on 2026-03-08 (version a1), remaining 50.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: pay
  cut 2026-06-10
u15: 600.00 PLN
  pinned: w = 2026-03-15
  unfulfilled: pay
  cut 2026-06-10
undone: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-20) not precise enough for the booking cut of pay" (pay)
  unknown day: w
  unfulfilled: pay
  cut 2026-06-10
undone_f: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-20) not precise enough for the booking cut of pay" (pay)
  unknown day: w
  unfulfilled: pay
  cut 2026-06-10
